  "unresolved_questions": [
    "PWR-002 requires >=600 mA LDO capability while PWR-003 caps VBUS draw at 500 mA: is the 600 mA figure a device rating headroom target (assumed here) or an actual load requirement that would exceed the USB default sink limit?",
    "Should a USB-to-UART bridge (e.g. CP2102/CH340) be added, or is programming done via the ESP32-WROOM-32 pins/external header only? The pin table exposes USB_D+/USB_D- directly on U1, which ESP32-WROOM-32 (no native USB) cannot use for USB 2.0 - this likely needs either a bridge IC or reassignment of these pins to UART0.",
    "The 110 x 65 mm outline is far larger than needed for this component count; is the size fixed by an enclosure, or may it shrink to reduce the bare-board cost against COST-001?",
    "Is any ESD protection on USB D+/D- and the I2C bus in scope, given the <=20 BOM line-item ceiling?",
    "Should GPIO25 (present in the pin table but unassigned) be left as a test point, a status LED, or a no-connect?",
    "Confirm the USB-C receptacle variant (16-pin USB 2.0 vs 24-pin full) and whether VCONN/SBU handling is required."
